\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One edge}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Let the graph consist of two vertices and one edge. The
Laplacian in the definition of the
[spectral dimension](fdip-00CO) sends a pair of values
#{(f,g)} to #{(f-g,g-f)}. The constant pair has eigenvalue
#{0}, and #{(1,-1)} has eigenvalue #{2}. The heat trace is
#{Z(t)=1+\ue^{-2t}}, and the spectral dimension is
##{d_s(t)=\frac{4t}{\ue^{2t}+1}.}
As #{t} tends to #{0}, the denominator tends to #{2} and the
numerator tends to #{0}, so #{d_s(t)} tends to #{0}. As
#{t} tends to infinity, #{0<d_s(t)\le 4t\ue^{-2t}}, which also
tends to #{0}.}
